---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["What is the default DKIM canonicalization?", "The default is simple/simple if the c= tag is not specified in the DKIM-Signature header. Most providers default to relaxed/relaxed instead."], ["Can I mix simple and relaxed?", "Yes, the c= tag can specify different algorithms for headers and body independently (e.g., c=relaxed/simple). But relaxed/relaxed is recommended."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "DKIM Canonicalization",
  description: "DKIM canonicalization explained: simple vs relaxed algorithms for headers and body, and why forwarding breaks simple.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "DKIM Canonicalization" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DKIM Canonicalization: simple vs relaxed Header and Body Algorithms (RFC 6376)"
  description="DKIM canonicalization explained: simple vs relaxed algorithms for headers and body, and why forwarding breaks simple."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DKIM Canonicalization</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DKIM Canonicalization</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-dim">DKIM canonicalization explained: simple vs relaxed header and body algorithms, and why forwarding breaks simple.</p>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'></th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>simple</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>relaxed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Header canonicalization</td><td>Exact match including all whitespace and folding</td><td>Collapses whitespace, removes trailing empty lines, lowercases header names</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Body canonicalization</td><td>Exact match including trailing empty lines</td><td>Collapses multiple spaces, removes trailing empty lines, strips trailing whitespace</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Survives forwarding?</td><td>No: any modification breaks the hash</td><td>Yes: tolerant of minor reformatting</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Recommended</td><td>No (too fragile)</td><td>Yes (standard choice)</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>DKIM canonicalization is the process of normalizing an email message's headers and body into a standard form before computing the cryptographic hash, defined in RFC 6376 Section 3.4.</p><p class='mt-3'>Two algorithms exist for each of headers and body: simple (no modification, exact match) and relaxed (whitespace collapsing, header name lowercasing, trailing whitespace removal).</p><p class='mt-3'>Relaxed canonicalization is recommended because simple canonicalization breaks whenever an intermediate server modifies whitespace or refolds headers, which is common during email forwarding.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">If your DKIM verification fails only for forwarded or mailing-list emails, check the c= tag in the DKIM-Signature header. If it says simple/simple, switching to relaxed/relaxed in your email provider's DKIM settings will fix most forwarding failures.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the default DKIM canonicalization?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The default is simple/simple if the c= tag is not specified in the DKIM-Signature header. Most providers default to relaxed/relaxed instead.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I mix simple and relaxed?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, the c= tag can specify different algorithms for headers and body independently (e.g., c=relaxed/simple). But relaxed/relaxed is recommended.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
